<title>USA: Scripps Trust asks court for stock flexibility.</title>
<headline>Scripps Trust asks court for stock flexibility.</headline>
<dateline>CINCINNATI 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trustees of The Edward W. Scripps Trust said Wednesday they have asked the Butler County, Ohio probate court to approve their interpretation of the trust agreement's language that requires the trust to &quot;insure&quot; its control of the E.W. Scripps Co.</p>
<p>The company said approval of the Trust's request would allow the E.W. Scripps Co greater flexibility in the use of its stock for acquisitions and mergers.</p>
<p>The trust currently holds 82 percent of the company's common voting stock, which is not publicly traded, and 53 percent of its publicly-traded class A common stock.</p>
</text>
